<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 11.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 11.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Jan 11 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Jan 5 - Jan 11</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,629,742 tns	167,013 tns    10.25 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,601,152 tns	165,709 tns    10.35 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,478,891 tns	150,975 tns    10.21 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Jan 11</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     7,335,999 tns	716,036 tns     9.76 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     6,489,600 tns	604,457 tns     9.31 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     6,875,552 tns	655,872 tns     9.54 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 56 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 54 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 53 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9530</p>
</text>
